      "format": "markdown",
      "text": "# Field notes\n\nThe survey team reached the northern ridge on the third day. Snow had closed the lower pass, so the route ran along the eastern face instead.\n\n> Radio contact was lost for six hours.\n\n## Findings\n\nThree of the five markers were intact and matched their recorded positions. The fourth had been moved about ten metres downhill by a rockfall, and its base plate was cracked. The fifth could not be found, although the team searched the slope below it for most of an afternoon. A replacement marker will be set on the next visit, once the pass is open.\n"
    }
  },
